libwebp 1.5.0's decoder, as released
(https://storage.googleapis.com/downloads.webmproject.org/releases/webp/libwebp-1.5.0.tar.gz,
SHA-256 7d6fab70cf844bf6769077bd5d7a74893f8ffd4dfb42861745750c63c2a5c92c),
for OpenCiv2's own HD pictures (src/platform/hd_image.c).  Only what
WebPDecodeRGBA needs, the files of libwebpdecoder's plain C: src/dec/*,
src/dsp's COMMON_SOURCES (no SSE2, NEON, MIPS or MSA variants), src/utils's
COMMON_SOURCES, and the headers they include (src/webp/*.h,
src/enc/histogram_enc.h, backward_references_enc.h).  src/webp/config.h is
OpenCiv2's: compiled with HAVE_CONFIG_H (tools/build_native.py), it turns
off the instruction-set variants and threads.  Licence: COPYING and PATENTS
(THIRD-PARTY.txt, 14.).
